# Static Example Pages

Prefer static HTML for example page chrome. TypeScript should only mount widgets into hosts that already exist in the document.

## Do

- Put toolbars, headings, intros, forms, links, and widget host containers (`#…-host` divs) in HTML files (`index.html`, `discover/index.html`, etc.).
- In `main.ts` / `render*.ts`, `querySelector` those hosts and call `mountWidget` / layout factories.
- For extra routes, add a separate HTML entry and register it in Vite `build.rollupOptions.input` (see calendar `discover/index.html`).

## Do not

- Build page structure with `document.createElement`, `innerHTML`, or `root.replaceChildren()` for toolbars, sections, or host divs.
- Wipe `document.body` and recreate an alternate page in JavaScript.

## Exception

Dynamic DOM inside `xorlab/src/renderer/Widget.ts` (and card / segment renderers) is expected — that is the widget tree, not example page chrome.

## Incorrect

```typescript
export function mountDiscoverPage(root: HTMLElement): void {
  root.replaceChildren();
  const host = document.createElement("div");
  host.id = "discover-monthly-horizontal";
  root.appendChild(host);
  mountWidget({ host, /* ... */ });
}
```

## Correct

```html
<!-- discover/index.html -->
<div id="discover-monthly-horizontal" class="widget-host"></div>
```

```typescript
export function mountDiscoverPage(): void {
  const host = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>("#discover-monthly-horizontal");
  if (!host) throw new Error("Discover page markup is missing required hosts.");
  mountWidget({ host, /* ... */ });
}
```
